    {
      "id": "b9b78524-3437-44f0-9756-d6f240966446",
      "name": "Why MCP is awesome",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / Why MCP is awesome",
      "docTypeId": "3aca80f2-c0da-477d-a822-a3cd21ab1bd9",
      "templateId": "66210d95-12d7-41c2-98be-5de5f68bfc69",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "title",
          "value": "Why MCP is awesome"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "summary",
          "value": "The Model Context Protocol gives AI agents one standard way to reach the tools and data they need, so you stop writing a bespoke integration for every system."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.DateTime",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "publishDate",
          "value": "2026-10-02 09:00:00"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "heroImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "c1000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a1",
              "mediaKey": "70fe5721-0ea2-40e3-9201-30d80dfe3db4",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "body",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "61f406a3-fecc-4040-997c-8fd28a12d051",
                "key": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>Every AI assistant that wants to do real work needs to reach outside its own chat window: to read a database, edit a document or change a website. Until recently, each of those connections was a one-off integration that worked with one assistant and one system.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "e80700b9-e28e-4672-b30a-ae16acc38cd6",
                "key": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "c1000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a2",
                        "mediaKey": "e6ebddf1-a186-4c70-89ec-589fb34c9ff0",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "caption",
                    "value": "Connected structure, photo by Alina Grubnyak on Unsplash"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "61f406a3-fecc-4040-997c-8fd28a12d051",
                "key": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>The Model Context Protocol (MCP) fixes that. It is an open standard that lets a server expose tools, data and prompts in one predictable shape, and lets any MCP-aware client discover and use them. Build the server once and every compatible agent can use it.</p><p>Three things make it feel like more than a tidy spec: tools describe their own inputs with schemas, so an agent can call them correctly without being told how; the protocol is the same whether the server fronts a filesystem or a CMS; and the agent acts on real content rather than just describing it.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "urls": [
        "/why-mcp-is-awesome/"
      ],
      "docType": "blogPost",
      "template": "blogPost"
    },
    {
      "id": "8101057c-80c2-4dba-96e2-45ffde89d33b",
      "name": "Why MCP is awesome, part 2: the agent in your CMS",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / Why MCP is awesome, part 2: the agent in your CMS",
      "docTypeId": "3aca80f2-c0da-477d-a822-a3cd21ab1bd9",
      "templateId": "66210d95-12d7-41c2-98be-5de5f68bfc69",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "title",
          "value": "Why MCP is awesome, part 2: the agent in your CMS"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "summary",
          "value": "This site was modelled, filled and checked by an AI agent talking to Umbraco over MCP. Here is what that looked like and why it matters."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.DateTime",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "publishDate",
          "value": "2026-10-05 09:00:00"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "heroImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "c2000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a1",
              "mediaKey": "e9ee7e6e-0389-4a1a-9f8d-a509f96c07b6",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "body",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "b2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "b2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "b2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "61f406a3-fecc-4040-997c-8fd28a12d051",
                "key": "b2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>Here the protocol earns its keep. This site was modelled, populated and checked by an agent talking to Umbraco through its MCP server: document types, data types, templates, media and content, all created through tool calls.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "e80700b9-e28e-4672-b30a-ae16acc38cd6",
                "key": "b2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "c2000000-0000-4000-8000-0000000000a2",
                        "mediaKey": "ddd23abf-957d-4fc9-84b7-abc8ed709714",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "caption",
                    "value": "Puzzle hands, photo by Vardan Papikyan on Unsplash"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "61f406a3-fecc-4040-997c-8fd28a12d051",
                "key": "b2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>The useful part is the feedback loop. The agent reads back what it wrote, and the server exposes each document type's schema, so the agent does not have to guess property aliases or block shapes.</p><p>MCP is not a magic wand. It is a clean contract between an agent and a system it can actually operate, and that contract is what made the rest of this site possible.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "b2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "b2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "b2000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "urls": [
        "/why-mcp-is-awesome-part-2-the-agent-in-your-cms/"
      ],
      "docType": "blogPost",
      "template": "blogPost"
    }
